        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "1548eb89-060b-5dc6-886e-007c10b11e76",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Gordon Waller, Paul McCartney, Norman Newell, Del Davis\n- Organizations: EMI\n- Groups: Peter and Gordon, Lennon–McCartney\n- Works: \"A World Without Love\", \"Mellow Dubmarine\"\n- Roles: singer-songwriter-guitarist, A&R manager\n\nFacts:\n- Gordon Waller was born on 4 June 1945 and died on 17 July 2009.\n- Gordon Waller was a British singer-songwriter-guitarist.\n- Gordon Waller was best known as Gordon in the 1960s pop duo Peter and Gordon.\n- \"A World Without Love\" was the biggest hit by Peter and Gordon, and it reached No. 1 and sold one million copies.\n- Paul McCartney wrote \"A World Without Love,\" and the song was credited to Lennon–McCartney.\n- Norman Newell worked as an A&R manager for EMI.\n- At EMI, Norman Newell worked with Peter and Gordon and artists including Shirley Bassey, Claude François, Vera Lynn, Russ Conway, Bette Midler, Judy Garland, Petula Clark, Jake Thackray, Malcolm Roberts, and Bobby Crush.\n- Del Davis recorded a cover of \"World Without Love\" that was featured on \"Mellow Dubmarine\".",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "5c2dff34-d05f-5e6d-a9a8-935be1adbbaa",
        "text": "Page: Gordon Waller. Sentence: Gordon Trueman Riviere Waller (4 June 1945 – 17 July 2009) was a British singer–songwriter–guitarist, best known as Gordon of the 1960s pop music duo Peter and Gordon, whose biggest hit was the No. 1 million-selling classic \"A World Without Love\".\nPage: A World Without Love. Sentence: The song was written by Paul McCartney and attributed to Lennon–McCartney.\nPage: Del Davis (singer). Sentence: His cover of \"World Without Love\" was featured on \"Mellow Dubmarine\".\nPage: Norman Newell. Sentence: As an A&R manager for EMI he worked with musicians such as Shirley Bassey, Claude François, Vera Lynn, Russ Conway, Bette Midler, Judy Garland, Petula Clark, Jake Thackray, Malcolm Roberts, Bobby Crush and Peter and Gordon.",
